#!/bin/sh
# Compact st-reflow help in a temporary floating terminal.

tmp=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/st-reflow-help.XXXXXX") || exit 1

cat > "$tmp" <<'EOF'
st-reflow quick help
====================

Copy / paste
------------
CLIPBOARD workflow:
  1. Select with mouse drag, Alt+drag for a rectangle, or copy mode (`v` regular,
     `V` line-wise, Ctrl+V rectangular). In mouse-aware apps, use Shift+Alt+drag.
  2. Ctrl+Shift+C copies and preserves trailing spaces/tabs.
     Ctrl+Shift+X copies and trims trailing spaces/tabs from every selected line.
     In copy mode, `y` copies normally and `Y` performs the trimmed copy directly.
     Explicit copies clear the highlight; successful y/Y/Ctrl+Shift+X also exit
     copy mode. PRIMARY and CLIPBOARD remain available; scrollback stays put.
  3. Ctrl+Shift+V pastes CLIPBOARD.

PRIMARY is the current mouse selection and is initially untrimmed. Paste it with
middle click, Ctrl+Shift+Y, or Shift+Insert. Ctrl+Shift+X replaces both PRIMARY
and CLIPBOARD with the trimmed selection, so either kind of paste is then clean.

Paste line endings are normalized for every program run inside st: LF, CRLF, and
CR each become one terminal Enter. This avoids doubled blank lines from CRLF.

Selection
---------
Drag mouse 1             regular selection
Double click             select word
Triple click             select logical/wrapped line
Alt + drag               rectangular selection
Shift + Alt + drag       rectangular selection when an app has mouse mode
Shift + mouse selection  force terminal selection when an app has mouse mode
Middle click             paste PRIMARY selection

Scrollback
----------
Mouse wheel              scroll history four lines
Shift+Mouse wheel        send shifted PageUp/PageDown to application
Shift+PageUp/PageDown    scroll one page
Alt+PageUp/PageDown      scroll one page
Alt+Up/Down              scroll one line
Alt+U / Alt+D            scroll one page

Font size
---------
Ctrl+Shift+PageUp/Down   increase / decrease font size
Super+Shift+= / -        increase / decrease font size
Ctrl+Mouse wheel         increase / decrease font size
Ctrl+Shift+Home          reset font size

Copy mode
---------
Alt+Escape               enter / leave Vim-style copy mode
h j k l / arrows         move
w / e / b                next word / word end / previous word
W / E / B                same, whitespace-delimited WORDs
0 / $ (Home / End)       row start / end
^ / %                    first / last printable character
gg / G                   oldest history / live cursor
[count]gg / [count]G     go to physical history row
Numeric prefix          repeat movement (5j, 3w, 2$)
Ctrl+u / Ctrl+d          half page up / down
PageUp / PageDown        page up / down
v / V                    visual / visual line
Ctrl+v                   visual rectangular block
y                        yank selection and exit copy mode
Y / Ctrl+Shift+X        clean yank and exit (trim trailing spaces/tabs)
Esc/q/i/Enter/Ctrl+c     leave copy mode

Copy mode works on both screens. Alternate-screen motions stay within visible
rows (no scrollback); gg goes to the top visible row, and counts address visible
rows. The display remains live. Resizing or switching screens exits copy mode.

Helpers
-------
Alt+L                    choose and open URL from history
Alt+Y                    choose and copy URL from history
Alt+O                    choose and copy one nonempty history line
Alt+F4                   close terminal; confirm if a process is running

Other shortcuts
---------------
Break                    send break
Ctrl+Print               toggle printer mode
Print / Shift+Print     print selection / screen (intercepted by dwm)
Ctrl+Shift+NumLock       toggle application keypad handling

Notes
-----
Help viewer: arrows/PgUp/PgDn scroll, / searches, q closes.
Search ignores case unless the pattern contains an uppercase letter.
less wraps long lines; do not use its -S option for this help.
st cannot tell whether the foreground program is bash, an editor, or another
interactive app. Paste normalization therefore applies to every paste into st.
EOF

st -c StHelp -n st-help -T 'st-reflow help' -g 92x34 \
	-e sh -c 'LESS= less -R -i "$1"; rm -f "$1"' sh "$tmp" &
